course: dictionary
lesson: 10310
title: Tower: a building, a stack, and a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tower is a tall, narrow building, like a castle tower or a clock tower. It can also be a tall stack of things, like a tower of blocks. Both meanings have the same idea: something narrow and high.
explain: Tower can also be a verb. To tower over something means to be much taller than it. «Peregrines hunt pigeons from the cathedral tower» tells you the tower is high enough for a bird to see far across the city. A tower is tall, so you can picture it easily.
explain: Towers help in maths and building too. If a tower has 6 blocks and each block is 3 cm tall, its height is 6 × 3 = 18 cm. To compare two towers, subtract the shorter height from the taller one to find the difference.
fact: A tower is a tall, narrow building, or a tall stack of things.
fact: «Tall towers are struck by lightning many times a year.»
fact: To tower over something means to be much taller than it.
fact: The verb forms are tower, towers, towered and towering.
fact: Height of a stack = number of blocks × height of one block.
exercise: «Peregrines hunt pigeons from the cathedral tower.» What is a tower here? | A pile of wet leaves | A deep hole in the ground | A soft cushion | *A tall, narrow building
exercise: Ben builds a tower of 6 blocks, and each block is 3 cm tall. How tall is his tower? | 3 cm | *18 cm | 9 cm | 24 cm
exercise: «The giraffe towered over the fence.» What does towered over mean? | Was much shorter than | *Was much taller than | Fell down on | Ran away from
test: A child builds a tower of blocks. What does tower mean here? | A tall, narrow building | *A tall stack of things | A small wooden box | A kind of bird
test: «A towering oak stood in the park.» What does towering tell you about the oak? | *Very tall | Very wet | Very small | Very old
exam: In «The tall boy towered over his friends», what does towered over mean? | Was much shorter than them | Hid behind them | Ran away from them | *Was much taller than them
